s. First-term incumbent Monica De La Cruz faces Tejano singer Bobby Pulido, a well-funded challenger drawing national attention and seven figures in outside spending. Expert raters are split between Tossup and Lean R, while recent polls and prediction markets lean toward Pulido.\n\nThe race remains genuinely competitive. De La Cruz has the incumbency and cash advantages, but Pulido's name recognition and the Democratic investment in the district have put the incumbent on defense. The forecast gives Pulido a modest edge, with enough uncertainty that a small shift in turnout or messaging could flip the race.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.4454, "margin": -0.75}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.6234, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.6548, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6308, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.5679, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6942, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6077, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.6479, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7065, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.6601, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.6541, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.6766, "margin": 2.5}]}